/*
Problem: Largest Number After Mutating Substring (LC 1946)
Topic: Greedy

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

We are allowed to mutate only one
continuous substring.

To maximize the final number:

• Ignore digits that would become
  smaller.

• Start mutating at the first digit
  that becomes larger.

• Continue mutating while the mapped
  digit is greater than or equal to
  the original digit.

• Stop immediately when a mapped digit
  becomes smaller, since the substring
  must remain continuous.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Traverse the number from left to
   right.

2. Before mutation starts:

   • If mapped digit > current digit,
     start mutation.

3. After mutation starts:

   • Replace digits while
     mapped >= current.

   • Stop when mapped < current.

4. Return the modified string.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

num = "132"

change =

1→9
3→8
2→5

Process:

1 → 9 (start)

3 → 8

2 → 5

Answer:

"985"

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

num = "021"

change:

0→0
2→1
1→1

0 → same

2 → smaller

1 → same

Mutation never starts.

Answer:

"021"

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Changing an earlier digit has a much
greater impact than changing a later
digit.

Therefore, we start mutation at the
first beneficial position.

Once mutation has started, stopping
and restarting is not allowed because
only one contiguous substring may be
mutated.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Single traversal of the string.

Space : O(1)

Only a boolean flag is used.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Greedy
*/

class Solution {
public:
    string maximumNumber(string num,
                         vector<int>& change) {

        bool started = false;

        for (int i = 0; i < num.length(); i++) {

            int digit = num[i] - '0';

            // Start mutation
            if (change[digit] > digit) {

                num[i] = change[digit] + '0';
                started = true;
            }

            // Continue mutation
            else if (change[digit] == digit &&
                     started) {

                num[i] = change[digit] + '0';
            }

            // End mutation
            else if (change[digit] < digit &&
                     started) {

                break;
            }
        }

        return num;
    }
};
